### Ethics approval

This study involved no human participants, human material, or human data. The corpus consists exclusively of a historical text in the public domain — Daniel Paul Schreber's *Memoirs of My Nervous Illness* (1903). Ethics approval was therefore not required and no informed consent was necessary.

### Data and code availability

All code, derived data, and reproducibility materials for this study are openly available in a public version-controlled repository:

<https://github.com/bamilu/schreber-computational-workflow>

An archived version corresponding to the submitted manuscript is available via Zenodo:

<https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19153006>

The repository includes the curated textual corpus derived from Schreber's *Memoirs of My Nervous Illness*, the full R-based computational pipeline, Quarto manuscript files, and all figures and tables reported in the article. All transformations applied to the source text are documented within the repository.

*Note to Editor:* The repository URLs above are withheld from the main manuscript file to comply with double-blind peer review requirements. They are provided here on the title page for the Editor's reference and will be reinstated in the published version upon acceptance.

